<h2>Let=E2=80=99s disclose some secrets</h2>
<h3>Gitea</h3>
<p>You have access to the <code>app1</code> git via Gitaea, hosted on the <=
code>:3000</code> port of the target system. Having a keylogger, you know y=
our targeted developer=E2=80=99s Gitea login is <code>htb-stdnt:Test@123</c=
ode>.</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://academy.hackthebox.com/storage/modules/243/gitea.png=
" alt=3D"Gitea repository interface for &quot;htb/app1&quot; showing 16 com=
mits, 1 branch, and 0 tags. Options include creating a new file, uploading =
a file, and viewing via HTTP or SSH. The branch is set to &quot;master.&quo=
t;"></p>
<h3>Jenkins</h3>
<p>Your keylogger also revealed the Jenkins credentials <code>admin:c235899=
364c147f0ad586c4408b18765</code>.</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://academy.hackthebox.com/storage/modules/243/jenkins.p=
ng" alt=3D"Jenkins dashboard showing a project named &quot;htb&quot; with t=
he last success 9 days ago. Options include creating a new item, viewing bu=
ild history, and managing Jenkins. No builds are in the queue."></p>
<p>The first thing we need to do is find the secret we are looking for. If =
we go to the user settings for <code>admin</code>, there is a settings menu=
 that lists <code>Credentials</code>. There, we can see the variable <code>=
flag2</code> that we must extract. Jenkins has some built in protections th=
at prevent us from retrieving the actual value of <code>flag2</code> from t=
he <code>Credentials</code> menu; we can only <code>update </code>the value=
 with a new one, <code>delete </code>the value, or <code>move </code>it to =
a different scope.</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://academy.hackthebox.com/storage/modules/243/jenkins-c=
redentials.png" alt=3D"Jenkins credentials page showing a list of credentia=
ls with IDs and names, including admin, testuser, htb-student, and flag. Al=
l are stored in the global domain."></p>
<h3>Jenkinsfile</h3>
<p>Returning to Gitea, we can now edit the <code>Jenkinsfile</code> to extr=
act the secret. We are going to log it to the console. Commit the changes.<=
/p>
